# RV-B — the "dot-shorthand == longhand" property against future over-tightening:
# a LEGAL bare non-resource (`String`, CoW-eligible) `.Wrap(s)` where the source
# `s` stays LIVE afterwards. Per the CoW ownership table, a bare identifier at a
# constructor/enum-init boundary clones-if-live / moves-if-dead — here `s` is used
# again by `print(s)`, so the init CLONES and both `s` and the payload are valid.
# Accepts on both backends and both lanes; prints `hi` (the still-live source)
# then `hi` (the cloned payload). This pins the no-over-reject else-branch: a
# naive "reject every enum-init arg" tightening would break this.
enum E:
    Wrap(String)
    Empty

void main():
    String s = "hi"
    E e = .Wrap(s)
    print(s)
    match e:
        case .Wrap(inner):
            print(inner)
        else:
            print("none")
